new file mode 100644
index 0000000..de4cafd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/major_data_link_backend/PERFORMANCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Diagnosing a slow backend
+
+The backend logs its own latency. Everything below is greppable in Railway →
+Deployments → Logs. Nothing here logs request bodies, headers, query strings or
+query arguments.
+
+## 1. Read the startup lines first
+
+```
+[db] round-trip SELECT 1: min=4ms median=6ms max=9ms (n=5; ...)
+[db] DATABASE_URL does not set connection_limit / pool_timeout. ...
+```
+
+* **median above ~50 ms** → the service and the database are in different
+  regions. Every query pays that latency and a handler that runs N sequential
+  queries pays it N times, so *every* endpoint is slow with no single slow
+  query to blame. Fix: put Railway and Supabase in the same region.
+* **connection_limit / pool_timeout warning** → set them on `DATABASE_URL`
+  (see `.env.example`).
+
+## 2. Then look at what is slow under real traffic
+
+| Log prefix        | Meaning                                                              | Likely cause / next step |
+|-------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|
+| `[slow-request]`  | A whole request took ≥ `SLOW_REQUEST_MS`. Shows `db=<ms>/<n>q` and the slowest query. `CLIENT_GAVE_UP` = the app disconnected before the answer. | If `db` is small, the time is elsewhere (provider or CPU). If `db` is large with many `q`, the handler does too many sequential queries. |
+| `[slow-query]`    | One Prisma call took ≥ `SLOW_QUERY_MS`, as `Model.action`. The time includes waiting for a pool connection. | One model repeatedly → missing index / big scan. Many unrelated models at once → pool exhaustion or network. |
+| `[slow-upstream]` | A provider/gateway call took ≥ `SLOW_UPSTREAM_MS`.                    | Provider is slow; nothing to fix locally. |
+| `[upstream-timeout]` | A provider call was abandoned at its ceiling.                     | Purchases are flagged for `/admin/provider-reconciliation`, never auto-refunded. |
+| `[event-loop]`    | Node's single thread was blocked (p99 ≥ 100 ms).                      | CPU-bound work. `bcryptjs` at cost 12 is pure JS and runs on every PIN check and login; if this fires under load, move to native `bcrypt`. |
+
+## 3. Reading a `[slow-request]` line
+
+```
+[slow-request] POST /api/data/purchase status=200 total=4210ms db=180ms/9q slowest=Transaction.create:60ms
+```
+
+Total 4.2 s but only 0.18 s in the database → the time was spent outside it
+(here: waiting on the provider). Compare `total` with `db` before touching SQL.
